# Staging must never be indexed. Every page's canonical points at
# https://briansmasonry.net/, so an indexed copy of this preview would compete
# with the client's live site under a second hostname.
#
# The rule is scoped to the staging hostname on purpose. At the domain cutover
# the client's real domain is attached to THIS SAME Worker, and an unscoped
# `/*` rule would carry the noindex onto the production site and quietly
# deindex the business.
#
# This lives in public/ so it survives every future deploy. The previous build
# served a noindex header from a `_headers` file that existed only inside the
# build output and not in git, so the first redeploy silently dropped it.
#
# Cloudflare only applies these to STATIC asset responses — /api/contact is
# served by the Worker script and sets its own headers.
https://staging.briansmasonry.net/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
